.TH TRUE 1 "2026" "ntlibc" "ntlibc User Commands"
.SH NAME
true \- do nothing, successfully
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B true
.RI [ operand ] .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B true
exits with a return status that indicates successful completion. It
can be invoked with any combination of options and operands; all are
ignored.
.PP
This is the standalone
.B true
utility
.RB ( obj/bin/true.exe ),
sharing its whole implementation with the identically-named
.I sh
built-in
.RI ( "src/sh/builtin.c" ),
via
.B __util_true_main()
in
.BR src/util/true.c .
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH OPERANDS
None; any operands given are ignored without error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Always.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
while true; do
    echo "looping forever"
done
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR false (1),
.BR test (1)
